    <string name="tg">&lt;b>Metadata block&lt;/b>&lt;br /> The metadata must follow the format:&lt;br /> &lt;tt> // ==UserScript==&lt;br /> // @key value&lt;br /> // ==/UserScript== &lt;/tt> &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@name&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The name of the userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@namespace&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The combination of &lt;tt>@namespace&lt;/tt> and &lt;tt>@name&lt;/tt> is the unique identifier for a userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@match/@exclude-match&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: Define rules to decide whether a script should be executed. It is recommended to use &lt;tt>@match&lt;/tt> instead of &lt;tt>@include&lt;/tt>. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@include/@exclude&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The old way to decide whether a script should be executed. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@version&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The version of the userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@description&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The description of the userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@require&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The require of the userscript. For example, &lt;br />&lt;tt>// @require https://my.cdn.com/jquery.js&lt;/tt>. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@run-at&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: Decide when the script will execute. &lt;tt>document-start&lt;/tt> is used to inject scripts before the page loads, &lt;tt>document-end&lt;/tt> is used to inject scripts after page load. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@grant&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: Specify which special GM_* APIs should be granted and can be used when the script executes.&lt;br /> &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@downloadURL&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The URL the script can be downloaded from. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@supportURL&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The support URL of the userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>&lt;tt>@homepageURL&lt;/tt>&lt;/b>: The homepage URL of the userscript. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>GM_* APIs&lt;/b>&lt;br /> &lt;tt>GM_*&lt;/tt> are a group of special APIs provided by Web. Currently supported special APIs include: &lt;br/> &lt;tt>GM_getValue/GM_setValue/GM_deleteValue/GM_listValues/GM_getResourceText/GM_getResourceURL/GM_addElement/GM_addStyle/GM_setClipboard/GM_xmlhttpRequest/GM_download/GM_registerMenuCommand/GM_unregisterMenuCommand&lt;/tt>. &lt;br />&lt;br /> &lt;b>Matching&lt;/b>&lt;br /> &lt;tt>@match&lt;/tt> defines a URL matching rule. &lt;tt>@exclude-match&lt;/tt> defines a match rule but used to exclude the matched URLs, similar to &lt;tt>@exclude&lt;/tt>. &lt;br />&lt;br /> For example:&lt;br /> &lt;tt> // @match https://www.google.com/something &lt;br /> // @match https://www.google.com/any/* &lt;br /> // @exclude-match https://www.google.com/any/not_me &lt;/tt> &lt;br />&lt;br /></string>
